  "diagnosis_text": "Confirmed: **h1 \u2192 h5 is failing (3/3 ICMP lost)**.\n\nThe fault is the inter-switch connection **s3 port 1 \u2194 s4 port 2**:\n\n- It is absent from ONOS\u2019s active topology (only 4 of the configured 5 inter-switch links are discovered).\n- `s3-eth1` is **disabled**.\n- `s4-eth2` is **disabled**.\n- Other adjacent host paths work: h1\u2194h2 and h4\u2194h5 both ping successfully, so neither endpoint attachment is indicated as faulty.\n\nThis breaks the forwarding path currently installed for h5: on s1, traffic destined to h5\u2019s MAC is sent out **port 1 toward s2**, i.e. along `s1 \u2192 s2 \u2192 s3 \u2192 s4 \u2192 s5`. It therefore reaches the disabled s3\u2013s4 segment. Although the physical `s1\u2013s5` link is up, it is not the path selected by the current flow rules.\n\n**Diagnosis:** failed/administratively disabled **s3\u2013s4 link**, specifically `s3:1` / `s4:2`; restore that link or update forwarding to use the viable s1\u2013s5 path.",
